      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/coker/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The area that became Coker was part of land ceded by the Creek Indians after the 1814 Treaty of Fort Jackson, opening it to European-American settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
